rms",name=S[545],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=21,l2=21,tree="Arms",name=S[601],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=22,l2=24,tree="Arms",name="Deep Wounds",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=25,l2=25,tree="Arms",name=S[622],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=26,l2=28,tree="Arms",name=S[602],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=29,l2=30,tree="Arms",name="Impale",r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=31,l2=32,tree="Arms",name="Bloodthrill",r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=33,l2=33,tree="Arms",name=S[702],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=34,l2=38,tree="Arms",name=S[846],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=39,l2=40,tree="Arms",name=S[832],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=41,l2=41,tree="Arms",name=S[747],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=42,l2=46,tree="Fury",name="Cruelty",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=47,l2=51,tree="Fury",name=S[623],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=52,l2=56,tree="Fury",name="Enrage",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=57,l2=57,tree="Fury",name=S[624],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=58,l2=58,tree="Fury",name=S[802],r1=1,r2=1,max=2},{l1=59,l2=60,tree="Protection",name=S[781],r1=1,r2=2,max=2}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[546]},{t="p",s="legend",x="|cff71d5ffBlue text was updated for the WoW Forever hotfixes up to 10 November and is awaiting final review.|r"},{t="h1",x="Arms",sub=S[637]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Swing a slow two-hander, keep Rend on your target so Bloodthrill opens extra Overpowers, and lead with Mortal Strike from level 40. Sweeping Strikes and Cleave let you kill two enemies at once."},{t="pills",list={S[562],S[607]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[748]},{t="h2",x=S[467]},{t="p",x="These stages describe a practical route toward the level-60 build. Arms fights from Battle Stance with a two-handed weapon the whole way; the stance dance only comes in for interrupts, Whirlwind and defensive cooldowns."},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Rend, Overpower and Charge"},{t="p",x="Open with Charge and fight in Battle Stance with the best two-hander you can find. Improved Heroic Strike (10–12) makes Heroic Strike 3 Rage cheaper, Improved Rend (13–15) makes Rend worth its Rage, and Improved Overpower adds 50% critical strike chance to Overpower after a dodge. Do the level 10 class quest for Defensive Stance, Sunder Armor and Taunt. Tactical Mastery, trained at 14, keeps 10 Rage when you change stance; Improved Tactical Mastery (16–18) keeps up to 15 more."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Two targets at a time"},{t="p",x="Slam and Victory Rush arrive at 20. Deep Wounds (22–24) adds a bleed to your critical strikes, Spearing Strike at 25 is a cheap extra hit that does much more to Giants, Dragonkin and mounted targets, and Two-Handed Weapon Specialization (26–28) adds 6% damage with a two-hander. Bloodthrill (31–32) gives main-hand hits on a Rend target a 20% chance to enable Overpower, and Sweeping Strikes at 33 copies your next five attacks to a second enemy, so pool Rage, pull two and Cleave. Weaponmaster follows (34–38), and Improved Slam 2/2 (39–40) stops Slam from delaying your swing and shortens its cooldown."},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Mortal Strike"},{t="p",x="Mortal Strike at 40 becomes your main attack and cuts healing on the target by 50%. Weaponmaster rewards whichever weapon type you hold, so pick weapons by damage per second. The last points go into Cruelty, Unbridled Wrath, Enrage, Reckless Swings (extra Rage on your next four swings for 25% of your base health) and Improved Execute in Fury, plus Improved Bloodrage in Protection. Plate armor is trained at 40."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[504]},{t="h2",x=S[562]},{t="p",x=S[65]},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[569]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[485]},{t="p",x=S[119]},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="Arms in Forever is built around Rend: Bloodthrill turns your main-hand hits on a Rend target into extra Overpowers, so keep Rend on whatever you are hitting. Weaponmaster replaces the old weapon specializations: axes and polearms gain 5% critical strike chance, maces and staves ignore 15% of armor, and swords can trigger an extra attack. Precision no longer exists, so all of your hit comes from gear."},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[660]},{t="h2",x=S[527]},{t="p",x="Your two-handed weapon is your most important item: Mortal Strike, Overpower, Slam and Whirlwind all scale with it. After that come hit, expertise, critical strike and Strength."},{t="h3",x=S[725]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[596],x="a slow two-hander"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Strength",x=S[703]},{t="stat",i=3,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Agility",x=S[726]},{t="p",s="small",x="A slower two-hander hits harder per swing at the same damage per second. Rage from normal swings is normalized in Forever: more damage does not mean more Rage, but critical auto attacks give double Rage."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[596],x="and speed"},{t="stat",i=2,b="Hit chance",x="to 8%"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Expertise",x="to 6.5%"},{t="stat",i=4,b=S[813],x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Strength",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Agility can beat Strength when an item has about 1.5 times as much of it. Haste and attack power are useful extras."},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[82]},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[528]},{t="h2",x=S[588]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority guide, not a fixed loop. Before Bloodthrill at 31, Sweeping Strikes at 33 and Mortal Strike at 40, leave out the steps you have not unlocked."},{t="h4",x="Open with Charge"},{t="p",x="Keep Battle Shout up and use Bloodrage between pulls so you start with Rage. Charge from Battle Stance generates Rage and stuns for 1 second. If several enemies stand together, pull one with a ranged weapon instead."},{t="h4",x="Rend, then Overpower"},{t="p",x="Apply Rend to anything that will live through most of it, and do not refresh it on a dying target. Use Overpower the moment it lights up, after a dodge or from Bloodthrill. It costs 5 Rage, cannot be dodged, blocked or parried, and Improved Overpower gives it 50% extra critical chance. Switching targets loses the proc."},{t="h4",x="Mortal Strike on cooldown"},{t="p",x="From 40, Mortal Strike is your main attack: weapon damage plus a bonus, 30 Rage, 6-second cooldown, and 50% less healing on the target for 10 seconds. Keep enough Rage for it after Rend and Overpower."},{t="h4",x="Slam with spare Rage"},{t="p",x="Slam costs 15 Rage. Before Improved Slam, cast it straight after an auto-attack because it resets your swing. With Improved Slam it no longer interrupts or delays your swing, and at 2/2 its 15-second cooldown drops to 10 seconds."},{t="h4",x="Two enemies: Sweeping Strikes and Cleave"},{t="p",x="Pool Rage on one target, heal up, then pull two. Sweeping Strikes (30 Rage) copies your next five attacks to a second enemy|cff71d5ff, and keeps its charges when no second enemy is hit|r; Cleave and Slam are cheap ways to spend them. Put Rend on both so either can trigger Bloodthrill. Whirlwind needs Berserker Stance and is best saved for group pulls."},{t="h4",x="Execute and Heroic Strike"},{t="p",x="Execute works below 20% health and spends all your remaining Rage. While questing, let auto-attacks finish weak enemies and keep the Rage; on dungeon bosses use Execute freely. Heroic Strike and Cleave replace your next swing and stop it generating Rage, so use them only when Rage is high."},{t="abil",names={S[747],"Overpower","Rend","Slam",S[702],"Cleave","Execute","Charge"}},{t="h3",x=S[789]},{t="p",x="Weapon damage comes first: Mortal Strike, Overpower, Slam and Whirlwind all scale with it, and a slower two-hander hits harder per swing at the same damage per second. After that look for hit, critical strike, Strength and Agility. Strength gives 2 attack power per point; Agility gives critical chance, dodge and armor but no attack power for a Warrior."},{t="p",x="Use the references below as candidate lists. Warriors use every melee weapon type plus bows, guns, crossbows and thrown weapons; you still need the weapon skill, so train it before you switch types. Plate is trained at level 40; until then mail is your heaviest armor."},{t="h3",x=S[439]},{t="p",x="Victory Rush is your only self-heal, so carry food and First Aid bandages. Sharpening stones on blades and axes, or weightstones on maces and staves, add flat damage to every hit. Rage and Strength consumables help most in dungeons."},{t="p",x="Battle Shout raises attack power for your group, Demoralizing Shout and Thunder Clap reduce the damage you take, and Sunder Armor helps every physical attacker. Shield Bash needs a shield; Pummel needs Berserker Stance from 38. Keep Hamstring for runners."},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[638]},{t="h2",x=S[440]},{t="p",x=S[61]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[41]},{t="macro",n=S[498],x=S[206],code=S[268]},{t="macro",n=S[608],x=S[154],code=S[259]},{t="macro",n=S[704],x=S[326],code=S[275]},{t="macro",n=S[710],x=S[195],code=S[295]},{t="macro",n=S[589],x=S[218],code=S[253]},{t="macro",n=S[499],x=S[226],code=S[351]},{t="macro",n=S[500],x=S[156],code=S[305]},{t="macro",n="Ranged pull",x=S[237],code=S[171]},{t="macro",n=S[515],x=S[166],code=S[276]},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Rend",x="Spread Rend across two targets during Sweeping Strikes so either can trigger Bloodthrill.",code="#showtooltip Rend\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Rend"},{t="macro",n="Mortal Strike / Shift Execute",x="Normal press casts Mortal Strike. Hold Shift for Execute when the target is below 20%.",code="#showtooltip\n/cast [mod:shift,harm,nodead] Execute; [harm,nodead] Mortal Strike"},{t="macro",n="Sweeping Strikes + Cleave",x="Activates Sweeping Strikes and queues Cleave on your next swing. Cleave is a next-swing attack, so it does not wait for the global cooldown.",code="#showtooltip Sweeping Strikes\n/cast Sweeping Strikes\n/cast Cleave"},{t="macro",n="Shield up / Shift two-hander",x="Swap to a one-hander and shield for Shield Bash or Shield Wall; hold Shift to swap back. Replace the three item names with your own.",code="#showtooltip\n/equip [mod:shift] Your Two-Hander\n/equipslot [nomod] 16 Your One-Hander\n/equipslot [nomod] 17 Your Shield"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[318]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[711]},{t="h2",x=S[486]},{t="p",x=S[67]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[68]},{t="p",s="notice",x="Warrior loot selection · 30 October 2026. Mail and plate armor, shields, cloaks and jewelry, every melee weapon type, and bows, guns, crossbows and thrown weapons; Intellect-, Spirit- and spell-only pieces are excluded. Shields are hidden on the Arms page. Rarity and acquisition confidence remain separate."},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[529]},{t="h2",x=S[483]},{t="p",x=S[81]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[570]},{t="h2",x=S[468]},{t="p",x=S[35]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[530]},{t="h2",x=S[426]},{t="p",x=S[36]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[497]},{t="kicker",x=S[712]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[101]}}},{id="fury",name="Fury",token="FURY",gearBrackets={{b="Quest rewards",no="Quest rewards that fit this spec's stat priority, sorted by quest level. The tooltip names the quest, its level, the quest giver and the faction. Quest level is not the minimum pickup level.",keys={"st-warrior-2","st-warrior-1","warrior-g129","warrior-g136","warrior-g76","warrior-g103","warrior-g26","warrior-g65","warrior-g73","warrior-g140","warrior-g142","warrior-g171","warrior-g49","warrior-g220","warrior-g131","warrior-g37","warrior-g44","warrior-g84","warrior-g137","warrior-g208","warrior-g14","warrior-g1","warrior-g95","warrior-g135","warrior-g156","warrior-g9","warrior-g119","warrior-g170","warrior-g3","warrior-g32","warrior-g159","warrior-g197","warrior-g27","warrior-g39","warrior-g100","warrior-g206","warrior-g18","warrior-g40","warrior-g80","warrior-g81","warrior-g128","warrior-g139","warrior-g205","warrior-g59","warrior-g75","warrior-g104","warrior-g105","warrior-g222","warrior-g34","warrior-g53","warrior-g96","warrior-g154","warrior-g46","warrio