=S[587]},{id="questgear",x=S[544]},{id=S[497],x=S[709]}},asideNote=S[83],talentString="30303213102000000050530055102100231",ranks={{tree="Arms",name=S[484],r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[669],r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[462],r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[545],r=2,max=2},{tree="Arms",name=S[601],r=1,max=1},{tree="Arms",name="Deep Wounds",r=3,max=3},{tree="Arms",name=S[622],r=1,max=1},{tree="Arms",name="Impale",r=2,max=2},{tree="Fury",name="Cruelty",r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name=S[623],r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name=S[790],r=3,max=3},{tree="Fury",name="Enrage",r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name=S[691],r=5,max=5},{tree="Fury",name=S[624],r=1,max=1},{tree="Fury",name=S[708],r=2,max=2},{tree="Fury",name="Death Wish",r=1,max=1},{tree="Fury",name=S[782],r=2,max=2},{tree="Fury",name="Flurry",r=3,max=3},{tree="Fury",name="Bloodthirst",r=1,max=1}},order={{l1=10,l2=12,tree="Arms",name=S[484],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=13,l2=15,tree="Arms",name=S[669],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=16,l2=18,tree="Arms",name=S[462],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=19,l2=20,tree="Arms",name=S[545],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=21,l2=21,tree="Arms",name=S[601],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=22,l2=24,tree="Arms",name="Deep Wounds",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=25,l2=25,tree="Arms",name=S[622],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=26,l2=27,tree="Arms",name="Impale",r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=28,l2=32,tree="Fury",name="Cruelty",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=33,l2=37,tree="Fury",name=S[623],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=38,l2=40,tree="Fury",name=S[790],r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=41,l2=45,tree="Fury",name="Enrage",r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=46,l2=50,tree="Fury",name=S[691],r1=1,r2=5,max=5},{l1=51,l2=51,tree="Fury",name=S[624],r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=52,l2=53,tree="Fury",name=S[708],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=54,l2=54,tree="Fury",name="Death Wish",r1=1,r2=1,max=1},{l1=55,l2=56,tree="Fury",name=S[782],r1=1,r2=2,max=2},{l1=57,l2=59,tree="Fury",name="Flurry",r1=1,r2=3,max=3},{l1=60,l2=60,tree="Fury",name="Bloodthirst",r1=1,r2=1,max=1}},blocks={{t="anchor",id="overview"},{t="p",s="eyebrow",x=S[546]},{t="h1",x="Fury",sub=S[637]},{t="p",s="lede",x="Dual wield from level 20, gain Rage from both weapons, and hit with Whirlwind and Bloodthirst from Berserker Stance, with Reckless Swings and Death Wish for extra Rage and burst."},{t="pills",list={S[563],S[607]}},{t="anchor",id="journey"},{t="kicker",x=S[748]},{t="h2",x=S[467]},{t="p",x="These stages describe a practical route toward the level-60 build. Warriors learn Dual Wield at 20, so Fury uses a two-hander until then. From level 40 you can keep Protection as a second specialization for tanking."},{t="p",s="level",x="1–19 · Rend, Overpower and Rage"},{t="p",x="Use a two-hander in Battle Stance with Charge, Rend and Overpower. The first points go into Arms: Improved Heroic Strike (10–12), Improved Rend (13–15), Improved Tactical Mastery (16–18) to keep more Rage when you change stance, and Improved Overpower (19–20). Do the level 10 class quest for Defensive Stance, Sunder Armor and Taunt. Tactical Mastery, trained at 14, keeps 10 Rage when you change stance."},{t="p",s="level",x="20–39 · Two weapons"},{t="p",x="Train Dual Wield at 20. Anger Management (21), Deep Wounds (22–24), Spearing Strike (25) and Impale (26–27) finish the Arms points, then Cruelty (28–32) adds 5% critical strike chance, Unbridled Wrath (33–37) gives your weapon hits a chance to generate extra Rage, and Furious Precision (38–40) adds up to 10% hit to off-hand attacks. Berserker Stance comes from your level 30 class quest, Whirlwind is trained at 36 and Pummel at 38."},{t="p",s="level",x="40–60 · Bloodthirst"},{t="p",x="Enrage (41–45) and Dual Wield Specialization (46–50, 50% more off-hand damage) come next, then Reckless Swings (51), Improved Berserker Rage (52–53), Death Wish (54), Improved Whirlwind (55–56, a shorter cooldown and more damage to the closest enemy) and Flurry (57–59, 30% attack speed for three swings after a critical strike). Bloodthirst completes the build at 60. Plate armor is trained at 40."},{t="anchor",id="talents"},{t="kicker",x=S[504]},{t="h2",x=S[563]},{t="p",x=S[65]},{t="widget",w="talents"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[569]},{t="widget",w="ranks"},{t="h4",s="summary",x=S[485]},{t="p",x=S[119]},{t="widget",w="order"},{t="p",s="notice",x="Off-hand attacks miss much more often than main-hand ones, which is why Furious Precision exists: it adds 10% hit to off-hand attacks only. Whirlwind already strikes with both weapons in Forever, and Improved Whirlwind shortens its cooldown by 2 seconds and adds 30% damage to the closest enemy. Reckless Swings costs 25% of your base health for 5 extra Rage on each of your next four swings."},{t="anchor",id="stats"},{t="kicker",x=S[660]},{t="h2",x=S[527]},{t="p",x="Fury wants strong weapons first, then hit and expertise so your attacks land, then critical strike and Strength. Crits also feed Flurry and Rage."},{t="h3",x=S[725]},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[596],x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Strength",x=S[703]},{t="stat",i=3,b="Stamina",x=""},{t="stat",i=4,b="Agility",x=S[726]},{t="p",s="small",x="Rage from normal swings is normalized in Forever: more damage does not mean more Rage, but critical auto attacks give double Rage."},{t="h3",x="At level 60"},{t="stat",i=1,b=S[596],x=""},{t="stat",i=2,b="Hit chance",x="to 8%"},{t="stat",i=3,b="Expertise",x="to 6.5% from behind"},{t="stat",i=4,b=S[813],x=""},{t="stat",i=5,b="Strength",x=""},{t="p",s="small",x="Weapon skill is rare in Forever but very strong when you find it; some estimates put it first, up to 305. Dual wielding raises the miss chance of white hits, so extra hit still helps."},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[82]},{t="anchor",id="combat"},{t="kicker",x=S[528]},{t="h2",x=S[588]},{t="p",x="Treat this as a priority guide, not a fixed loop. Before Dual Wield at 20, Whirlwind at 36 and Bloodthirst at 60, leave out the steps you have not unlocked."},{t="h4",x="Charge, then Berserker Stance"},{t="p",x="Keep Battle Shout up and use Bloodrage between pulls. Charge from Battle Stance, then switch to Berserker Stance: Tactical Mastery keeps up to 10 Rage through the switch, and the stance adds 3% critical strike chance but 10% more damage taken."},{t="h4",x="Bloodthirst on cooldown"},{t="p",x="From 60, Bloodthirst (30 Rage, 6-second cooldown) deals damage equal to 45% of your attack power plus a flat amount, and gives 10% movement speed for 10 seconds."},{t="h4",x="Whirlwind on cooldown"},{t="p",x="Whirlwind (25 Rage, 10-second cooldown, 8 seconds with Improved Whirlwind, Berserker Stance) hits up to four enemies within 8 yards with both weapons. Use it on single targets too once Bloodthirst is on cooldown. Before 36, keep Rend and Overpower from Battle Stance instead."},{t="h4",x="Overpower after a dodge"},{t="p",x="When the target dodges, swap to Battle Stance and use Overpower; Improved Overpower gives it 50% extra critical chance. Swap back afterwards. Only do this when the stance change will not throw away pooled Rage."},{t="h4",x="Execute and spare Rage"},{t="p",x="Execute works below 20% health and spends all your remaining Rage, so use it when it will kill or on a boss. With Rage to spare, queue Heroic Strike, or Cleave on two targets; both replace a swing and stop it generating Rage."},{t="h4",x="Cooldowns"},{t="p",x="Death Wish adds 20% Physical damage and Fear immunity for 30 seconds but raises damage taken by 5%. Berserker Rage breaks Fear and Incapacitate and gives extra Rage from hits taken. Recklessness at 50 doubles your critical strike chance for 15 seconds at the cost of 20% more damage taken. Piercing Howl slows everything nearby when you need to get away."},{t="abil",names={"Bloodthirst","Whirlwind","Execute","Heroic Strike","Death Wish","Berserker Rage","Intercept","Pummel"}},{t="h3",x=S[789]},{t="p",x="Weapon damage per second comes first on both weapons. A slow main hand makes Bloodthirst-free swings and Whirlwind hit harder; the off hand can be faster. Hit matters more for Fury than any other Warrior build because off-hand attacks miss so often, then critical strike for Flurry and Enrage, then Strength and Agility."},{t="p",x="Use the references below as candidate lists. Main Hand weapons cannot go in your off hand; pair them with a One-Hand weapon. Plate is trained at level 40; until then mail is your heaviest armor."},{t="h3",x=S[439]},{t="p",x="Victory Rush gives you some healing in fights, but food and bandages still cover the gaps. Keep sharpening stones or weightstones on both weapons. Rage potions help most during Death Wish and Recklessness."},{t="p",x="Battle Shout raises attack power for your group and Demoralizing Shout reduces damage taken. Pummel works in Berserker Stance without a shield from 38; before that, equip a shield for Shield Bash. Intercept closes gaps in combat from 30."},{t="anchor",id="macros"},{t="kicker",x=S[638]},{t="h2",x=S[440]},{t="p",x=S[61]},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[41]},{t="macro",n=S[498],x=S[206],code=S[268]},{t="macro",n=S[608],x=S[154],code=S[259]},{t="macro",n=S[704],x=S[326],code=S[275]},{t="macro",n=S[710],x=S[195],code=S[295]},{t="macro",n=S[589],x=S[218],code=S[253]},{t="macro",n=S[499],x=S[226],code=S[351]},{t="macro",n=S[500],x=S[156],code=S[305]},{t="macro",n="Ranged pull",x=S[237],code=S[171]},{t="macro",n=S[515],x=S[166],code=S[276]},{t="macro",n="Whirlwind / switch to Berserker",x="In Berserker Stance this casts Whirlwind. In any other stance the first press switches stance; press again to Whirlwind.",code="#showtooltip Whirlwind\n/cast [stance:3] Whirlwind; Berserker Stance"},{t="macro",n="Bloodthirst / Shift Execute",x="Normal press casts Bloodthirst. Hold Shift for Execute when the target is below 20%.",code="#showtooltip\n/cast [mod:shift,harm,nodead] Execute; [harm,nodead] Bloodthirst"},{t="macro",n="Bloodrage into Death Wish",x="Bloodrage first for the Rage, then Death Wish. If Bloodrage is on cooldown the macro still casts Death Wish.",code="#showtooltip Death Wish\n/cast Bloodrage\n/cast Death Wish"},{t="macro",n="Mouseover Hamstring",x="Slow a runner under your pointer without changing targets, before it reaches more enemies.",code="#showtooltip Hamstring\n/cast [@mouseover,harm,nodead][harm,nodead] Hamstring"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[318]},{t="anchor",id="dungeons"},{t="kicker",x=S[711]},{t="h2",x=S[486]},{t="p",x=S[67]},{t="widget",w="rarity"},{t="p",s="notice",x=S[68]},{t="p",s="notice",x="Warrior loot selection · 30 October 2026. Mail and plate armor, shields, cloaks and jewelry, every melee weapon type, and bows, guns, crossbows and thrown weapons; Intellect-, Spirit- and spell-only pieces are excluded. Shields are hidden on the Fury page. Rarity and acquisition confidence remain separate."},{t="widget",w="loot"},{t="anchor",id="professions"},{t="kicker",x=S[529]},{t="h2",x=S[483]},{t="p",x=S[81]},{t="widget",w="prof"},{t="anchor",id="crafting"},{t="kicker",x=S[570]},{t="h2",x=S[468]},{t="p",x=S[35]},{t="widget",w="craft"},{t="anchor",id="questgear"},{t="kicker",x=S[530]},{t="h2",x=S[426]},{t="p",x=S[36]},{t="widget",w="quest"},{t="anchor",id=S[497]},{t="kicker",x=S[712]},{t="h2",x="Your notes"},{t="widget",w="notes"},{t="p",s="small",x=S[101]}}},{id="protection",name="Protection",token="PROT",gearBrackets={{b="Quest rewards",no="Quest rewards that fit this spec's stat priority, sorted by quest level. The tooltip names the quest, its level, the quest giver and the faction. Quest level is not the minimum pickup level.",keys={"st-warrior-3","warrior-g129","warrior-g216","warrior-g31","warrior-g103","warrior-g73","warrior-g140","warrior-g142","warrior-g150","warrior-g223","warrior-g226","warrior-g37","warrior-g44","warrior-g60","warrior-g62","warrior-g84","warrior-g194","warrior-g208","warrior-g178","warrior-g14","warrior-g95","warrior-g135","warrior-g148","warrior-g156","warrior-g9","warrior-g119","warrior-g147","warrior-g170","warrior-g3","warrior-g72","warrior-g159","warrior-g197","warrior-g27","warrior-g39","warrior-g82","warrior-g144","warrior-g13","warrior-g18","warrior-g40","warrior-g45","warrior-g80","warrior-g81","warrior-g117","warrior-g130","warrior-g13